> Zero-cost ties, unreachable vertices and invalid input

For equal tentative costs, the heap’s smaller vertex id settles first,
regardless of the order of the source’s adjacency entries. In the next
example, the source lists vertex 2 before vertex 1, both at cost one.
Vertex 1 nevertheless settles first and supplies vertex 3’s parent. Zero
cycles and duplicate arcs produce inspections, but equal candidates never
push new entries. Vertex 4 is isolated, so its distance is infinity and
its reconstructed route is empty.

A negative edge invalidates the settling proof. In a separate three-node
control, 0→1 costs two, 0→2 costs five and 2→1 costs minus six.
An irrevocable settlement of vertex 1 at cost two would be premature:
the route through vertex 2 costs minus one. Dijkstra rejects that graph;
the existing Bellman–Ford API returns minus one. This illustrates the
broken invariant, rather than claiming an unchecked variant must return
one particular wrong answer.

All endpoints and weights are checked, including arcs in unreachable
components, before adjacency allocation. NaN, either infinity and negative
weights raise invalid_argument. If an examined sum of finite nonnegative
costs overflows, the kernel raises overflow_error, even when the candidate
would not beat an already known shorter route. It does not silently turn
a reachable cost into the infinity marker. A finite DBL_MAX route is valid.

The public two-field ShortestPathResult layout is unchanged. Safe path
recovery now bounds traversal and validates visited indices, finite
nonnegative distances, vector alignment and cycles. Out-of-range and
positive-infinity targets retain the original empty-return convenience.
Without a stored source or edge list, this function checks structural
safety; it cannot certify that a manually supplied sentinel is the intended
source or that arbitrary parent costs satisfy edge recurrences.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dijkstra_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::tuple<std::size_t,std::size_t,double>> edges{{0,2,1},{0,1,1},{1,3,0},{2,3,0},{3,2,0},{3,3,0},{0,1,1},{1,0,0}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::dijkstra_trace(5,edges,0);
  std::print("Zero-cycle control: distances {}; settled {}; parent of 3 is {}; unreachable route length {}.\n",t.result.distance,t.settled_order,t.result.predecessor[3],dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(t.result,4).size());
  std::print("Inspections {}; improvements {}; stale removals {}.\n\n",t.work.edges_examined,t.work.successful_relaxations,t.work.stale_pops);
  const std::vector<std::tuple<std::size_t,std::size_t,double>> negative{{0,1,2},{0,2,5},{2,1,-6}};
  const auto reference=dm::algorithms::bellman_ford(3,negative,0);
  std::size_t rejected=0;
  for(double w:{-1.,std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity(),std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()}){
    try{(void)dm::algorithms::dijkstra(3,{{1,2,w}},0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::dijkstra(3,negative,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  std::size_t overflow=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::dijkstra(3,{{0,1,1e308},{0,2,1},{1,2,1e308}},0);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++overflow;}
  std::size_t malformed=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::reconstruct_path(dm::algorithms::ShortestPathResult{{0,1},{dm::algorithms::kNoPredecessor,1}},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++malformed;}
  if(rejected!=4 || overflow!=1 || malformed!=1 || reference.distance[1]!=-1)return 1;
  std::print("Rejected weight controls {}; overflow controls {}; malformed-parent controls {}. Bellman-Ford negative-edge optimum {:.0f}.\n",rejected,overflow,malformed,reference.distance[1]);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(75,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.width=2;node.height=1.3;node.font_size=24;
  d.node("s",{0,0},"Source 0\ncost 0",node).node("early",{8,0},"Vertex 1\ntrue cost −1",node).node("later",{4,-3},"Vertex 2\ncost 5",node);
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke bad;bad.color={220,38,38};bad.width=3.5;
  d.edge("s","early","direct cost 2").edge("s","later","cost 5").edge("later","early","cost −6",bad)
   .text({4,2},"Negative-edge control: settling vertex 1 at cost 2 is premature",24)
   .text({4,-4.7},"Dijkstra rejects this graph; Bellman–Ford returns the route cost −1",21)
   .save_svg("build/dijkstra_boundaries.svg");
}
