> Count the work rather than infer it from a timing curve

Let R be the number of strict improvements, E_r the number of outgoing
arcs examined from reachable settled vertices and V_r the number of
reachable vertices. A full successful execution has

\[
\text{pushes}=\text{pops}=R+1,\qquad
\text{stale pops}=R+1-V_r,\qquad R\le E_r\le E.
\]

The extra push is the initial source entry. Every improvement creates one
entry, and draining the heap removes every entry. Each reachable vertex
accounts for one fresh removal; the rest are stale. The peak heap size is
at most R+1. Validation and adjacency construction still inspect/store all
E input arcs, including unreachable components.

Binary heap operations take logarithmic time in the live entry count.
Thus a safe multigraph bound is O(V+E+(R+1)log(R+2)), or
O(V+E+(E+1)log(E+2)) after eliminating R. Storage is O(V+E).
For simple graphs, E is at most quadratic in V, giving the familiar
O((V+E)log V) bound. The original report’s unrestricted heap-size/log-V
claim needs this distinction when arbitrarily many parallel arcs are allowed.
Counters count logical pushes, removals and inspections, not comparator
calls, elapsed time or a guaranteed constant per heap operation.

For a forward band, include u→u+d for d=1,...,w when the destination exists,
and give every arc cost one. With n>w, the exact edge count is
wn−w(w+1)/2. Every non-source vertex improves once, the heap peaks at w,
and delta(0,v)=ceil(v/w). The existing canonical band generator supplies
the inputs; no graph-building algorithm is reimplemented in the report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dijkstra_forward_bands.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> sizes,inspections,pushes,peaks;
  std::print("| vertices | band width | arcs / inspections | improvements | pushes / pops | stale | peak heap | last cost |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{32u,128u,512u,2048u}){
    const std::size_t w=8;const auto edges=dm::algorithms::dag_forward_band_edges(n,w);
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::dijkstra_trace(n,edges,0);
    if(t.work.edges_examined!=w*n-w*(w+1)/2 || t.work.successful_relaxations!=n-1 || t.work.heap_pops!=n || t.work.stale_pops || t.work.max_heap_size!=w || t.result.distance.back()!=(n-1+w-1)/w)return 1;
    sizes.push_back(n);inspections.push_back(t.work.edges_examined);pushes.push_back(t.work.heap_pushes);peaks.push_back(t.work.max_heap_size);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} |\n",n,w,t.work.edges_examined,t.work.successful_relaxations,t.work.heap_pops,t.work.stale_pops,t.work.max_heap_size,t.result.distance.back());
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.line(sizes,inspections,"edge inspections",{37,99,235}).points(sizes,inspections,"",{37,99,235},5).line(sizes,pushes,"heap pushes",{220,38,38});
  p.title("Actual work in width-eight forward bands").x_label("number of vertices").y_label("logical operation count").y_limits(0,22000).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dijkstra_forward_bands.svg");
}
```
